    <body period="#tg_1990">
      <article eId="art_1">
        <num>1</num>
        <heading>Supremacy of the Constitution</heading>
        <content>
          <p>This Constitution is the supreme law of Aurelia. Any law inconsistent with it is void to the extent of the inconsistency.</p>
        </content>
      </article>
      <article eId="art_14">
        <num>14</num>
        <heading>Private life</heading>
        <paragraph eId="art_14__para_1">
          <num>(1)</num>
          <content>
            <p>Every person has the right to respect for their private life, home and correspondence.</p>
          </content>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph eId="art_14__para_2">
          <num>(2)</num>
          <content>
            <p>The right in clause (1) may be limited only by a law that is necessary and proportionate to a legitimate aim.</p>
          </content>
        </paragraph>
      </article>
      <article eId="art_41">
        <num>41</num>
        <heading>Treaties</heading>
        <paragraph eId="art_41__para_1">
          <num>(1)</num>
          <content>
            <p>A treaty binds Aurelia when it is ratified by the President with the approval of Parliament.</p>
          </content>
        </paragraph>
        <paragraph eId="art_41__para_2">
          <num>(2)</num>
          <content>
            <p>A treaty forms part of the law of Aurelia only to the extent that it is given effect by an Act of Parliament.</p>
          </content>
        </paragraph>
      </article>
